# Bounded motion comparison — 8 October 2026

Current main `37fdbf8f` versus frozen PR239 `fe1487c1`. Both current bank bytes match the existing `77683c0c` comparison snapshot. Main has since merged the accepted faces. No tracked file or model was changed by this review.

Keep current main as the integration base. Do not choose one complete animation bank. Many body movements are the same; the useful differences are in the hand and arm fits.

| Action | Actual difference | Decision |
|---|---|---|
| Unarmed walk/run | Only 30 finger/thumb rotations differ. Root, torso, arm swing and legs agree within 0.1 degree / 0.1 mm. | Keep the gait. Judge relaxed hands separately on current bodies/all LODs. |
| Sabre/knife walk/run | Only 15 free-left-hand finger rotations differ. Weapon arm/body/legs agree. | Keep the gait and weapon carry. No whole-clip replacement needed. |
| Eight sabre/knife strikes | Only right upperarm/lowerarm/hand and three thumb rotations differ. Body/free arm/legs/contact timing agree. Current physical wrist maxima 92–142 degrees; PR239 35 degrees. | Prefer PR239's six-channel correction as a narrow donor. Retain current body and gameplay support/contact fitting. Test paid contact/facing before integration. |
| Punch | Left arm, both finger rows and right hand differ; right power-arm path, torso and legs agree. Wrist bends are small in both. | No basis here to choose the whole old punch. Keep body drive/contact; compare fist/free-arm shape visually. |
| Rifle walk/run | Arm/finger fits differ; body and legs agree. Current wrist bends right 20–22 degrees / left 27–35 degrees; old right 29–33 / left 39–40. | Retain current rifle carry. Old carry has no clear measured benefit. |
| Pistol walk/run | Right arm and fingers differ; gait/free-arm swing agree. Current right bend 38–62 degrees; old 30–57. | Hold whole-clip replacement. The small gain needs actual item and visual checks. |
| Pistol fire | Right arm/fingers/head differ. Current bend 10–21 degrees; old 32–33. | Retain current firing fit unless matched contact/visual evidence shows a defect. |
| Rifle fire | Both arms/fingers/spine/head differ. Current right bend ≈60 degrees; old ≈34. | Old upper-body fit is a useful donor, but verify sight line, shoulder stock, palms and ready transitions on current equipment. |
| Pistol strike | Right arm/fingers/head differ. Current right bend 79–82 degrees; old 51–52. | Prefer a targeted old reach correction, with its required item-offset metadata and unchanged current impact checks. |
| Rifle butt strike | Both arm/finger/spine/head fits differ. Current right 101–102 degrees / left 97–106; old right 38–40 / left 65. | Old fit is the stronger anatomy donor. It uses sequential regrip plus exact item compensation. Do not copy rotations alone. Keep current whole-boot, facing and actual cap-contact limits. |
| Bayonet | Arm/finger/spine/head fits differ. Current right bend 60–66 degrees; old 47–61. | No clear whole-clip winner; current grip/point/contact review is still needed. |
| Prone pistol | Existing 240 Hz evidence: old aim/fire wrist ≈30 degrees, current 77–84. But old forearms hover 44–49 mm with no support patch; old reload penetrates floor 122–131 mm. | Use old wrist direction only as a donor. Reject a wholesale replacement. Keep current support and refit reload. |
| Standing heal | Root, torso, arms and legs all differ. | Keep current, as agreed in the integration review. This is not a hand-only replacement. |

All named standing actions have the same duration and contact/shot markers. The clip clocks do not favor either bank; spacing and naturalness still require actual motion review.

The physical wrist comparison uses the actual native elbow→wrist and wrist→middle-MCP directions on the same current body rig at 120 Hz, plus exact markers. Large local quaternion changes are not treated as anatomical bend. This metric identifies folds; it does not prove naturalness, surface contact or gameplay correctness.

The unchanged focused blade checks pass **6/6 with PR239** and **4/6 with current main**. The current failures are the two native wrist-bound checks. Both sets pass forehand knuckles-down, backhand knuckles-up and forward thrust direction. The included grip check is loose 18 mm cylinder proximity, not exact paid-contact acceptance.

A matched actual-export backhand view at 0.466666667 s uses the same current Granadero body, equipment, light palette and isometric camera. Images and imported asset hashes are under `visual-current/` and `visual-pr239/`. These show a single peak pose, not a complete visual acceptance. The full-body camera is fixed; each hand close view uses the same hand-following framing rule.

The current hand visibly folds back into the cuff at this pose. PR239 keeps the hand outside the cuff and in a much straighter line with the forearm. Both full-body views retain the same stance, torso twist and free-arm position. The blade direction changes with the corrected hand, so exact runtime target-contact validation is still required. The existing cuff cutouts remain visible and are not fixed by this motion comparison.

- Current full body: `visual-current/granadero/stand.slash.blade.backhand.sample-1.png`
- PR239 full body: `visual-pr239/granadero/stand.slash.blade.backhand.sample-1.png`
- Current right hand: `visual-current/granadero/stand.slash.blade.backhand.sample-1.r-hand.png`
- PR239 right hand: `visual-pr239/granadero/stand.slash.blade.backhand.sample-1.r-hand.png`

## Evidence

- `independent-bounded-comparison.json`: exact selected channel allowlists, timings, metadata differences, body/bank pins and wrist metrics.
- `independent-channel-differences.json`: full numeric channel inventory.
- `independent-physical-wrists.json`: selected physical wrist measurements.
- `current-blade-check.log` and `pr239-blade-check.log`: focused test output.
- Existing prone proof: `/tmp/granaderos-prone-pistol-current-runtime-review/audit/pr239-prone-short-gun-native-comparison.json`.
- Existing heal comparison: `/tmp/granaderos-clinical-body-successor-f2e33df7/support-evidence/pr239-standing-heal-sampled-comparison.json`.

No 334-clip visual sweep or broad acceptance claim was made. Exact runtime target contact, support, held-item compensation, transition continuity and reduced-body hand surfaces remain required before any donor is integrated. Keep old body assets and runtime out of a motion-only transfer.
